# Build-context filter for the one repo-root-context image build
# (build-molecule-ci: `docker build -f docker/molecule-ci/Dockerfile .`).
# That Dockerfile COPYs only the two requirements files, so exclude
# everything else — the context upload stays a few KB instead of the whole
# repo. docker/ stays included so the Dockerfile itself remains in-context
# for non-BuildKit builders. Subdir-context builds (docker/<img>/) are
# unaffected by a root .dockerignore.
# NOTE: re-including a NESTED path (!ansible/requirements.yml) after `*`
# requires BuildKit (docker >= 23 default; CI's dind qualifies) — the classic
# builder prunes excluded parent dirs and would drop the file. Verified by
# building this context with a COPY of both files.
*
!requirements.txt
!ansible/requirements.yml
!docker/
